        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "the result of a perfect square expansion?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "i, v, ix",
          "worked": "Use $u^2+2uv+v^2=(u+v)^2$ or $u^2-2uv+v^2=(u-v)^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+8x+16&=(x+4)^2\\\\25-10x+x^2&=(x-5)^2\\\\4x^2+12x+9&=(2x+3)^2\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, i, v and ix.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q2-b-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "a difference of squares expansion?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "ii, iv, vii, x, xii",
          "worked": "Use $u^2-v^2=(u-v)(u+v)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2-16&=(x-4)(x+4)\\\\9-y^2&=(3-y)(3+y)\\\\4x^2-25&=(2x-5)(2x+5)\\\\64-49a^2&=(8-7a)(8+7a)\\\\36a^2-49b^2&=(6a-7b)(6a+7b)\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, ii, iv, vii, x and xii.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
